3. psycopg 3 (LGPL-3.0) - not distributed with this repository
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

psycopg is NOT listed in requirements.txt and is NOT included in this
repository. The desktop agent (agent/gpsource.py) imports it lazily, and only
when a Greenplum/PostgreSQL source is used. deploy/make-agent-kit.sh downloads
"psycopg[binary]" wheels from PyPI into an offline kit (deploy/agent_tools/).

If you build and hand out such a kit, you are redistributing psycopg, and the
LGPL-3.0 obligations apply to you: provide the license text and keep the
library replaceable by the recipient (the kit installs it as separate wheels,
which can be swapped). The binary wheels also bundle libpq and other native
libraries with their own licenses; check the wheel metadata before shipping.
This is a description of the situation, not legal advice.

